<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Investec yr shr, div jumps.</title>
<headline>Investec yr shr, div jumps.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended March 31 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>- headline diluted up 36.3 pct to 572.1 cts</p>
<p>    - attrib			581.0	  vs 447.0</p>
<p>    - attrib diluted	    557.6	  vs 419.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     260.0	  vs 200.0</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast diluted earnings per share at between 550.0 and 558.3 cents with consensus at 552.8.</p>
<p>They expected a dividend of between 250.0 and 269.0 cents, averaging out at 261.7.  </p>
<p>    Net income		   455.31	  vs 283.76</p>
<p>    Net interest income	586.95	  vs 346.40</p>
<p>    Other income		 661.68	  vs 404.92</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 55.711	  vs 40.95</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			515.24	  vs 317.17</p>
<p>    Tax			    102.34	  vs 68.21</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  10.336 charge vs none</p>
<p>Div payable June 20</p>
<p>On register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Investec Bank Ltd</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
